WEBVTT

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.020
The Azure Brigade folk are the ones
we can't be sure of yet.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.740
Even when they're being so welcoming?

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.090
They're just hoping to appease us.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.360
They probably don't want to get into 
conflict with the Seven-Light Faith

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.620
while they're exhausted from 
their battle against Gustave.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:24.480
If a battle breaks out, 
people will get hurt and die.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.220
If we can settle things diplomatically, 
that would be for the best.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.670
Tsukasa-san,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.620
do you think we'll be able to get along
with those in the Azure Brigade?

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.830
I'll cut right to the chase.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.300
It's impossible.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.980
But the new leader of that brigade, Conrad,
seems like a really good person.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.110
He's told an unforgivable lie.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.610
A lie, you say?

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.780
Yes.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.190
Remember the statue we need
to rebuild Gustave's lands?

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.370
When I asked where it was,
Conrad said he didn't know.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.620
However, that statue is likely 
already under his control.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.630
The movement of his eyes and tongue,
his expression...

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.550
All of it indicated that he was lying.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.840
So you're saying the Azure Brigade is 
trying to pocket that golden statue?

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.470
I knew it. I had a feeling that was the case.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.400
But if you already knew that,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.520
then why did you say
we'd bear the costs of the rebuild?

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.400
There are two reasons for that.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.030
The first is that we have yet
 to confirm Gustave's death.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.020
If he is still alive, then he'll be coming
to steal back that golden statue.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.670
I don't want something so dangerous
anywhere near us.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.160
The second is that publicizing
the Azure Brigade's corruption

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.540
won't do them any harm.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.200
Why's that?

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.570
Because, right now, public opinion 
in Gustave is with the Azure Brigade.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.300
Right?

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.430
Yeah.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:01.300
So the first thing we need to do is
get that public opinion on our side.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.860
Should our efforts to rebuild 
garner the trust of the people,

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.310
things will change.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.310
It'll be more effective to expose
 the Azure Brigade's corruption then.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:16.070
Until then, we'll let Conrad and the others 
line their own pockets all they want.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.740
After all, money can be taken back by force,
 unlike people's hearts.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:24.880
Now, with that plan in place,

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.080
let me give you all your directions.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.040
Could you please wait a moment?

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.080
I don't mind you handing out directions.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:32.880
But Tsukasa...

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.300
And you, Ringo...

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.450
I'm ordering you both to take five days rest.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.300
Huh?

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:46.000
The way I see it, both of you have remarkably 
weakened immune systems right now.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.070
If you keep going,

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.060
then Ringo will develop
 acute tonsillitis in five,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:53.560
and Tsukasa will collapse 
with bronchitis in seven.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.110
Both of which will require at least 
ten days for a full recovery.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.110
So you should both 
rest now while you can,

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.980
and focus on recovering.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:08.450
Seeing as you're the one prescribing it, 
Doctor Keine, I can't afford not to listen.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.720
It's good when patients listen.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.010
Man, the two who suck at 
taking breaks got hit good.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.170
Yeah.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.790
You should both take it easy.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.930
Uh-huh.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.790
Thank you.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.180
I know. Ringo.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.160
Since we're on break anyway,

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.600
why don't we tour the city
toward the end?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.220
Huh?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.380
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.450
<i>Bear?!</i>

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.750
<i>A date with Tsukasa, bear?!</i>

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:14.290
<b>It Seems Ringo's Worked Up 
\h\hthe Courage to Become a Hunter!</b>

